WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.182
A fluid interface crosses a layer of

00:00:03.182 --> 00:00:05.713
lung epithelial cells. This is the real

00:00:05.713 --> 00:00:08.245
chamber study, not a film of a

00:00:08.245 --> 00:00:08.968
patient's lung.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.425
A syringe pump drives liquid through a

00:00:18.425 --> 00:00:21.201
parallel plate chamber. The paper shows the

00:00:21.201 --> 00:00:23.976
actual apparatus and the glass surfaces supporting

00:00:23.976 --> 00:00:24.769
the cells.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.398
As the air liquid interface advances, local

00:00:33.398 --> 00:00:36.145
stresses reach the cell surface. The moving

00:00:36.145 --> 00:00:38.893
schematic explains the process; it is not

00:00:38.893 --> 00:00:40.463
a measured stress trace.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:48.497
These fluorescence images are from the original

00:00:48.497 --> 00:00:51.343
study. The unstressed control and the bubble

00:00:51.343 --> 00:00:54.190
exposed cells were stained with live and

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:55.003
dead markers.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:03.506
Across seven replicates, the stressed group showed

00:01:03.506 --> 00:01:06.363
about fifty three percent cell death, versus

00:01:06.363 --> 00:01:09.219
around zero to point two percent in

00:01:09.219 --> 00:01:11.667
controls. The difference was statistically significant.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.803
The study also stained actin filaments and

00:01:18.803 --> 00:01:21.957
nuclei. Here are its actual control and

00:01:21.957 --> 00:01:25.110
bubble exposure images, not synthetic fluorescence pictures.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:34.091
The single bubble did not produce a

00:01:34.091 --> 00:01:37.532
statistically significant change in actin organization, although

00:01:37.532 --> 00:01:40.972
the authors observed possible differences in filament

00:01:40.972 --> 00:01:41.464
orientation.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.640
The chamber makes an airway reopening problem

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.629
experimentally observable. It does not by itself

00:01:51.629 --> 00:01:54.619
establish what will happen to a patient

00:01:54.619 --> 00:01:55.473
during ventilation.
